01:35:19,253 --> 01:35:22,592
Does it have resource limits defined at all?

683
01:35:22,878 --> 01:35:28,721
Is it accidentally exposing a NodePort service directly to the internet when it was

684
01:35:29,008 --> 01:35:31,929
only ever supposed to be reachable internally?

685
01:35:32,216 --> 01:35:38,058
Every single control we've carefully built so far in this phase can be perfectly

686
01:35:38,345 --> 01:35:44,188
satisfied, completely and correctly, while the actual deployment manifest wrapped around all of it

687
01:35:44,474 --> 01:35:48,647
is still fundamentally, dangerously misconfigured in some other way entirely.

688
01:35:48,934 --> 01:35:54,777
Here's the mental model for this specific lecture, and it's the one that makes

