01:43:12,426 --> 01:43:18,269
who happens to be reviewing any particular pull request that day, is precisely your

775
01:43:18,555 --> 01:43:24,398
very first genuine batch of Rego policies waiting patiently to be written down formally.

776
01:43:24,685 --> 01:43:30,527
Let's also talk honestly about testing your actual policies themselves, because a policy with

777
01:43:30,814 --> 01:43:36,657
a subtle bug in its own underlying logic is arguably worse, in real practical

778
01:43:36,943 --> 01:43:42,786
terms, than having no policy at all in that specific area, precisely because it

